🧩 Analysis chain
Replace asyncio.Event with asyncio.Lock for true mutual exclusion in initialization

The asyncio.Event-based pattern allows concurrent initializations across all three classes. When _init_event is set(), all coroutines waiting on await _init_event.wait() wake simultaneously and proceed past the double-check—each sees _initialized=False and calls _initialize() concurrently. This defeats mutual exclusion and causes duplicate model loading/training and conflicting writes.

Fixes required in:

ml_predictor.py (lines 147–169): Replace _init_event with _init_lock; use async with self._init_lock: instead of event signaling
ai_engine.py (lines 344–345, 351–368): Same fix; replace _init_event with _init_lock
analyzer.py (lines 109–110, 112–129): Same fix; replace _init_event with _init_lock
